            <ArticleTitle>A rare cause of lumbosacral plexus neuropathy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>47-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This is the second report of a case in which a uterine myoma, one of the most common benign tumours of women, was the cause of a lumbosacral plexus neuropathy. The possibility of uterine myoma should be considered in the differential diagnosis of neuropathy of the lumbosacral plexus in women.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
